  "full_response": "Attention mechanisms are a key component of transformer models, which were introduced in a 2017 paper titled \"Attention is All You Need\" by Vaswani et al. The attention mechanism allows transformers to weigh the significance of different words in a sentence, enabling them to process sequences more effectively and capture dependencies across words, regardless of their distance from each other in the input sequence. Here's how it works:\n\n### Self-Attention:\n\n1. **Input Representation**:\n   - For a given input sequence, each word is initially represented as an embedding. In a transformer, this is typically concatenated with positional encodings to preserve the order information.\n\n2. **Query, Key, and Value Vectors**:\n   - Each input embedding is projected into three vectors using linear layers: Query (Q), Key (K), and Value (V). For a word \\( x_i \\) with embedding \\( z_i \\), these vectors are calculated as:\n     \\[\n     Q_i = W_Q \\cdot z_i, \\quad K_i = W_K \\cdot z_i, \\quad V_i = W_V \\cdot z_i\n     \\]\n   - \\( W_Q \\), \\( W_K \\), and \\( W_V \\) are learned weight matrices.\n\n3. **Scaled Dot-Product Attention**:\n   - For each word, compute the attention scores with every other word in the sequence. This is done by taking the dot product of the query vector of one word with the key vector of another word.\n   - Scores are scaled by the square root of the dimension of the key vectors to avoid extremely small gradients during training.\n     \\[\n     \\text{score}(i, j) = \\frac{Q_i \\cdot K_j^\\top}{\\sqrt{d_k}}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Attention Weights**:\n   - The raw scores are passed through a softmax function to obtain the attention weights, which represent the importance of each word relative to the others.\n     \\[\n     \\alpha_{i,j} = \\frac{\\exp(\\text{score}(i, j))}{\\sum_{k} \\exp(\\text{score}(i, k))}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Output**:\n   - Each word's output is computed as a weighted sum of the value vectors, using the attention weights.\n     \\[\n     \\text{Output}_i = \\sum_j \\alpha_{i,j} \\cdot V_j\n     \\]\n   - This output encapsulates information about the entire sequence,",
